            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nIt does respect environment configuration, just not some flags that are [enforced in command itself](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/9a92084b3e9595568c0b07b62ad3c43249fa91fb/lua/mini/pick.lua#L3416). The `--no-follow` flag is indeed enforced, but I don't quite remember the reason.\n\nThere was f39a455770aefdecda114370784c7dd7f9f7bf74 which adjusted flags to be as minimal as possible and I left `--no-follow` untouched. I'll take a look whether it was for performance reasons, strong opinion about results be part of `cwd`, or some technical issue.",
