            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> then it tells me this is the wrong tool for `files`, but i don't see any other way of configuring the fd behaviour other than flags like `--hidden` or `-H`.\n> \n> Am i doing something wrong?\n\nConfiguring of CLI tool behavior is recommended to be done via its own configuration approach. For `fd` the choice is [somewhat limited](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/256d35c9e24c9cf5f5da568e121e988c6ceb1e3f/doc/mini-pick.txt#L85C7-L85C68). I am not quite sure if there is a way to include `--hidden` as a part of currently supported `fdignore` files.\n\nAlso here is a relevant upstream issue: sharkdp/fd#362\n\nThis is one of the reasons why 'mini.pick' uses `rg` by default, because it allows proper [global configuration](github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/blob/master/GUIDE.md#configuration-file).",
